 ## Overview
-This method defines the training procedure for a Signed Distance Function (SDF) baseline network, specifically referred to as SDF-Instant-NGP in the source literature [S1]. It solves the problem of learning a continuous signed distance field from sparse or noisy geometric data by combining geometric supervision with physical regularization. It is distinguished from its parent method, [SDF Training with Eikonal Loss](2553-sdf-training-with-eikonal-loss.md), by the explicit inclusion of a sign loss term applied to free-space samples to enforce positive SDF values outside the surface, and by the specific hyperparameter configuration (batch size, learning rate, epochs) used for the SDF baseline in the RaDe-GS context [S1].
