 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **$\lambda$ Parameter**: The value of $\lambda$ for the sign loss is not specified in the source [S1]. Implementers must determine this via hyperparameter search or standard practices for sign losses in SDF training.
-*   **Gradient Computation**: The Eikonal loss requires computing the gradient of the network output with respect to the input coordinates. This must be done using automatic differentiation with `create_graph=True` to allow for second-order derivatives if needed, though first-order is sufficient for the norm calculation [S1].
-*   **Free Space Sampling**: The quality of the sign loss depends on the distribution of $\mathcal{X}_{\text{free}}$. If free space samples are too close to the surface, the sign loss may conflict with the SDF loss. If they are too far, the gradient may vanish. The source does not specify the sampling strategy for free space [S1].
